   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:28px;line-height:36px;border:none;padding:2px 0.14em 2px 0px;font-family:inherit;overflow:hidden;width:270px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span lang=\"en\" style=\"background-color:white\"><font color=\"#000000\">Dear all, first I would like to thank and congratulate you for this great tool.\n\nMy name is Andrew Matheus and I&#39;m relatively new to using GGIR, so I have a simple question. </font></span></span><div><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:28px;line-height:36px;border:none;padding:2px 0.14em 2px 0px;font-family:inherit;overflow:hidden;width:270px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span lang=\"en\" style=\"background-color:white\"><font color=\"#000000\">How to do analysis of different epochs? (ex: 1s, 10s, 15s, 30s, 60s)</font></span></span><div><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:28px;line-height:36px;border:none;padding:2px 0.14em 2px 0px;font-family:inherit;overflow:hidden;width:270px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span lang=\"en\" style=\"background-color:white\"><font color=\"#000000\">\nIs there a command line so I can choose the epochs, or should I generate files in different epochs like in ActiLife?</font></span></span></div><div><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:28px;line-height:36px;border:none;padding:2px 0.14em 2px 0px;font-family:inherit;overflow:hidden;width:270px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span lang=\"en\" style=\"background-color:white\"><font color=\"#000000\">\nAnd finally, if I can choose several epochs through a command, how will these results be generated?\n\nThank you in advance for your time.</font></span></span><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "RKL0MNizAAAJ",
   "from": "Vincent van Hees",
   "author": "017566be30afa7f3",
   "date": "2023-03-16T09:17:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] Modify epoch length",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Dear Andrew,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Epoch size is set with argument windowsizes. <span>Further, you can opt to aggregate this to 1 minute epoch in the part 5 analyses </span><br><span style=\"font-family:system-ui,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal;display:inline!important\">with argument part5_agg2_60seconds. <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline!important\">Further, time spent in MVPA is reported by default with 5, 60 and 300 second epochs in part 2. </span>S</span></span>ee package documentation for details:</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><span><a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489943411000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3eobOmimrBTkLWAVNCtNm3\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html</a></span><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><span><a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIRParameters.html\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIRParameters.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489943411000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0lYrmHAtv2j_iVdVodOesD\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIRParameters.html</a></span><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.875rem\">If you want to run GGIR with multiple epoch lengths, e.g. to study the effect of epoch length in more detail, then you will need to process the data multiple times.</span></div><div><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Note that we offer GGIR training courses to help new users get started:</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><span><a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" href=\"https://www.accelting.com/ggir-training/\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.accelting.com/ggir-training/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489943411000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DK9V1p-6ZORvtRsICKj8y\">https://www.accelting.com/ggir-training/</a></span><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Thanks,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Vincent</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(107,107,107)\">Dr. Vincent van Hees | Independent consultant | </span><a title=\"https://accelting.com/\" href=\"https://accelting.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://accelting.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489943411000&amp;usg=AOvVaw24kpy1-wVNawjcs51lOWSN\">https://accelting.com/</a><br></div><div><img alt=\"image\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/RpackageGGIR/attach/b3d830f4a244/image?part=0.1.1&amp;view=1\"><br></div>\r\n    </div>\r\n    \r\n            <div>\r\n        \r\n            </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div>\r\n        ------- Original Message -------</div>"
